WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.600
Improvements to accessibility in games

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.200
has become more of a focus over the

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.799
previous console generation

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.120
and thankfully great strides have been

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:10.719
made in opening up our favorite hobby

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.320
to many more people who require

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:14.960
additional considerations

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.320
in order to enjoy their experiences. Many

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.880
studios have dedicated

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.000
accessibility consultants in-house and

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.680
some games feature

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.920
options to tailor the experience to

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.519
accommodate for a raft of requirements

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.439
from high contrast options for the

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:29.199
vision impaired to offering alternative

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:33.120
control schemes for those with physical disabilities.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.600
I spoke to Steve Saylor, content creator

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.840
and video game accessibility consultant,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.760
and media editor at Can I Play That,

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.760
about what accessibility means

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.600
and the progress the industry has made

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.600
in improving it. 

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.800
Generally it's usually described

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.920
as settings or options that make a game

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.640
playable for those with disabilities

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.559
whether you're blind, deaf or hard of hearing, or

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:56.000
have motor disabilities,

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:58.800
there are settings that kind of will

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.399
enable those players to be able to

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.719
remove some of the barriers that they

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:03.280
may have with the abilities that they have

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.320
so that they can be able to play the same game

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.080
as their friends are playing, with the

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:12.960
same challenge that they have

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.720
without a disability.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.840
"Semi-auto rifle. Semi-auto rifle ammo.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.840
Nine loaded. Nine reserve."

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.520
We really didn't see anything for

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.840
accessibility in any game

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:25.360
The very first Assassin's Creed

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.080
game didn't even have subtitles

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:31.680
subtitles whereas now when you look at the

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.119
latest version Valhalla, it has far more

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.400
accessibility options

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:38.159
than the first game did, and so

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.840
it took a long time to be able to get to

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:41.759
this point but it really kind of ramped

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.680
up within the past few years where

00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:45.119
advocates like myself and consultants

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.840
like myself have been able to talk to developers

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.640
and encourage them to add these options

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.920
and talk to disabled players because

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.759
they want to be able to play those games

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.079
and not only is that sort of like a

00:01:53.759 --> 00:01:56.320
good thing to do

00:01:54.079 --> 00:01:57.920
but it also can translate

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:01.680
into sales as well.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:03.600
Now when we're going into next gen

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.680
we're seeing a lot more awareness of

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.200
accessibility and whether that's in part

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.920
because The Last of Us Part Two this year,

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.520
or just the momentum in general our

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.760
conversations are

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.440
becoming more prominent and a majority

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.520
of people know about accessibility

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.040
and a lot of those people are developers

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.080
and they want to be able to try to make

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.120
their games

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.800
available and for everyone.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.400
In recent years game developers and designers have

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.280
been more proactive about improving accessibility

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.120
and reaching out to advocates like Steve

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.120
who worked on The Last of Us Part 2

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:35.360
has been key to that.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.440
However, fundamentally each console has its own

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.760
accessibility challenges that many don't

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.599
think about and require more involvement

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.239
from platform holders and the industry

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:44.640
at large to address.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.680
In a twitter thread earlier this year,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.440
Steve called the 100 dollar difference in price

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.480
between the disc and digital editions of

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.560
the PS5

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.560
are disability tax citing the

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.280
PlayStation store's inflexible refund policy

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:58.800
as an issue for many gamers with

00:02:56.959 --> 00:02:59.680
accessibility requirements.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.879
Obviously there are two different

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.560
versions of the PlayStation 5, you have the

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:04.319
digital and the disc version.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.080
Generally a lot of disabled players

00:03:04.319 --> 00:03:08.640
usually prefer to

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:10.400
purchase the physical copy of a game

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.360
mainly because a lot of the refund policies

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.200
if you purchase the game digitally

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.959
are not at a place yet

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.879
where they can be able to at least get

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:20.640
their money back. Because often times

00:03:18.879 --> 00:03:24.000
whenever we have to be able to put down

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:26.959
60 dollars plus, that's a lot of money

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.480
for for some people to spend on a game,

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:30.400
and if a disabled player

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.680
pays that amount for a game, they take it

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.959
home and they play it,

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:37.599
and they realize an hour in

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:38.959
I can't play this, that's a lot of money

00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:41.360
to be able to kind of

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:42.319
in a way be wasted, and if you

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.440
buy it digitally

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:47.920
oftentimes the refund policy is 'Well

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:49.360
you already downloaded it so we can't

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.080
give you a refund.'

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.959
Whereas if we buy it physically, at least

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.400
we could be able to

00:03:52.959 --> 00:03:56.239
take it back to the store and even

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.920
though we can't get a full refund

00:03:56.239 --> 00:03:59.200
we more likely can be able to trade it

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:01.200
in to be able to at least get some of

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.720
our money back. When it comes to

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.319
sort of the disability tax i had

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.720
mentioned with the PS5,

00:04:04.319 --> 00:04:08.000
it basically costs in some cases

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.840
100 dollars more

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.000
to be able to have access to that.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.480
Also the ability to be able to use

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:18.239
Game Pass as a selling point for the new

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.759
is a huge accessibility advantage, because

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:21.680
like I mentioned in regards to

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.800
sort of the disability tax, what's great

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.680
about Game Pass

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.680
is that you can be able to get games day

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.000
one of release from Xbox first party studios.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.680
When you have the ablility to get

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.120
those games by paying a certain amount

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.400
per month, you could be able to download

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.800
those games day one

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.479
and you can play it try it out.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.759
If it doesn't work for you and you're

00:04:38.479 --> 00:04:42.080
not able to play it

00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:44.560
you can easily delete it, download a new one

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:46.960
and you're not wasting a huge amount of money for it.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:50.160
As consoles move towards an all-digital future,

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.080
and with accessibility features rarely

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:55.120
included in a game's marketing prior to launch,

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:57.840
subscription services such as Xbox Game Pass

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.000
become all the more important in ensuring that

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.560
gamers with individual requirements

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.800
don't end up unfairly out of pocket.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:07.280
Playstation does offer Playstation Now,

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.680
but its library is by comparison

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.800
skewed much more towards older games and

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:13.120
unlike Game Pass

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:15.199
does not generally include new 

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.639
first party titles upon release.

00:05:15.199 --> 00:05:18.800
There's also the Playstation Plus Collection

00:05:16.639 --> 00:05:20.320
but once again this consists

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:22.320
of last-gen games.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.000
Until accessibility features are common

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:26.080
as part of a game's marketing,

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.680
or Sony changes their refund policy to

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.759
account for accessibility,

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:32.000
it may continue to be gamers with those

00:05:29.759 --> 00:05:33.680
requirements who foot the bill.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.680
There are also considerations to be made

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.440
when it comes to the hardware itself.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:39.680
It's a mundane point but a larger,

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:41.919
heavier console, or one that requires you

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:43.600
to attach a stand with a small screw,

00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:45.680
means that many people with physical

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:47.919
disabilities may find themselves unable

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:49.680
to unbox and set up their new console

00:05:47.919 --> 00:05:51.440
without the assistance of someone else

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.880
which, given the world is currently in

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:55.520
the midst of a pandemic,

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:57.600
is far from ideal. 

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:59.199
A headline feature for the PS5

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:00.960
 is the brand new DualSense controller, 

00:05:59.199 --> 00:06:02.960
which features haptic feedback and adaptive triggers,

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.120
but these settings can be disabled on a

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:06.880
system level as well as individually in

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:09.600
titles such as Miles Morales,

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:11.360
which offers 'accessibility vibration.'

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:13.919
Frustratingly these additions mean that

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:17.039
the DualShock 4 and other PS4-compatible controllers

00:06:14.639 --> 00:06:18.639
are not supported for PS5 games, which

00:06:17.039 --> 00:06:20.000
will be a concern to those who have a

00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:22.720
personalized setup

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.160
adapted to old hardware. 

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:26.080
By contrast, Microsoft has ensured that any

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.919
compatible Xbox One generation

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.520
controller works without issue on the

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:31.440
Series X and S.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:33.039
As with the Xbox One you can remap

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.199
buttons on a system level

00:06:33.039 --> 00:06:37.360
and the Xbox Adaptive Controller is

00:06:35.199 --> 00:06:39.919
supported, along with the Adaptive Gaming Kit.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.520
Though Microsoft deserves plaudits for

00:06:39.919 --> 00:06:43.440
being the only major company with an

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:45.440
official adaptive controller, and the

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.880
only one selling additional third-party

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.560
solutions on its site,

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.880
it should be noted that the controller

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:53.599
and kit could set you back over 200 dollars,

00:06:51.599 --> 00:06:56.479
not including the external joysticks

00:06:53.599 --> 00:06:57.280
that are required. 

00:06:56.479 --> 00:06:59.440
For the Xbox Series X and S

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:01.440
what Microsoft did was, they actually

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:04.800
took a lot of what they had

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:07.919
already developed internally and refined it

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.560
for next generation. So if you're coming

00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:11.199
from an Xbox One

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:12.880
and you're using the

00:07:11.199 --> 00:07:15.520
accessibility settings

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:17.039
in the ease of access menu in the Xbox

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:19.440
it's the exact same

00:07:17.039 --> 00:07:21.919
ease of access menu on the Series X and S

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.759
and so you're going to get the same

00:07:21.919 --> 00:07:25.120
experience. That's on the Xbox side.

00:07:23.759 --> 00:07:25.680
On the PlayStation side actually, what they

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.440
did was kind of interesting.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:29.039
There's pretty much the same

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:31.520
settings that is on

00:07:29.039 --> 00:07:32.800
PlayStation 4 is on the PlayStation 5.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:35.759
They have also

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:38.560
kind of enhanced a lot for blind players

00:07:36.639 --> 00:07:40.000
Before there was a text-to-speech option in the

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.080
PlayStation 4

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.440
that unfortunately was only available in

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:44.000
English only. But now with the

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.400
PlayStation 5

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:50.080
they've enabled screen reader to be available

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:52.560
in multiple languages across the world, so

00:07:50.639 --> 00:07:54.400
you can be able to turn on the console

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:55.680
from day one when you get it, and it will

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.800
guide you through the setup process and

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.160
you can be able to keep that on

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.840
throughout the rest of your setup.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:01.599
"Fast 2. Fast 3."

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:03.599
It's an amazing way to be able to

00:08:01.599 --> 00:08:06.720
kind of navigate the system and it works flawlessly

00:08:04.479 --> 00:08:07.520
across the entire operating system of

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:10.560
the PlayStation.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:11.759
"Voice type. Voice volume."

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:13.039
When it comes to sort of like the DualSense

00:08:11.759 --> 00:08:15.680
controller that I have here

00:08:13.039 --> 00:08:17.280
with the haptic feedback it basically

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.319
adds a lot more immersion for blind

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:20.879
players as well,

00:08:18.319 --> 00:08:22.560
where the precise and subtle details of

00:08:20.879 --> 00:08:24.000
the vibrations in the controller

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:26.000
actually help blind players to be able

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:29.039
to feel the environment that they're

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:31.599
in, and know when they're walking or when they're

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:33.120
being attacked, or when things are kind of

00:08:31.599 --> 00:08:35.039
moving from side-to-side,

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:37.039
and that along with the 3D audio

00:08:35.039 --> 00:08:39.039
that's built into it is

00:08:37.039 --> 00:08:40.159
a really amazing feature.

00:08:39.039 --> 00:08:41.599
Actually PlayStation has a

00:08:40.159 --> 00:08:43.760
neat little feature in it called Game Presets

00:08:41.599 --> 00:08:44.959
where any game you play will

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:46.480
automatically turn on

00:08:44.959 --> 00:08:47.839
whatever difficulty setting you want to

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.720
be able to set, 

00:08:47.839 --> 00:08:51.200
whether to turn on subtitles,

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:52.720
or to invert controls, 

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:54.240
and enable settings that you normally would have to

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:55.920
turn on whenever you start up a game for

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:56.959
the first time. 

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:58.880
I'm really excited to be able to see

00:08:56.959 --> 00:09:00.720
what else that Sony and

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.800
Microsoft can be able to do

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:04.399
moving forward now that accessibility

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:06.640
is kind of built in

00:09:04.399 --> 00:09:08.000
from from the ground up. 

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:10.000
It's clear the industry has come a long way

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.760
in the past 10 years in recognizing the

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:14.160
challenges that some people face

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.680
just to be able to play games at all. 

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:17.360
But hopefully this is the beginning of a

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:19.920
progression towards a future

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:22.160
where all games are open to everybody

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:24.000
no matter their individual requirements.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:25.440
As far as for Xbox what I'd love to be

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.519
able to see from them, and they actually

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:29.120
are doing that, is internally in their

00:09:27.519 --> 00:09:31.519
studios they are pushing for

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:32.560
accessibility pretty much on every

00:09:31.519 --> 00:09:34.880
single project that

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:38.000
every studio is working on in their Xbox game studios,

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:39.760
and they have an internal accessibility

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:40.720
team called 'Gaming for Everyone'.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.720
I'd really love to be able to

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:44.240
see where that goes, and and I'm loving

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.680
what Xbox and

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:47.200
their initiatives have kind of done.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.600
What I would like to be able to see 

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.839
over the next

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:53.440
five to ten years for accessibility in games is...

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:54.720
I'm a content creator.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.800
So reviewing games is kind of

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:58.800
what I get to do. I would love it for the

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:00.800
industry to get to a point where

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:02.160
five years down the road I can be

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:04.720
sort of nitpicking

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:05.680
certain accessibility options, instead of

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:08.079
just saying

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:09.440
"Why doesn't this game have some?"

00:10:08.079 --> 00:10:11.839
That's what I would love to be able to get

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:13.120
get to that point, where every game

00:10:11.839 --> 00:10:16.160
has a standard of accessibility

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:18.240
and we can be able to

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:19.600
open this genre or this art form up to

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:21.440
more people. I love what

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:22.480
Microsoft put out a couple of

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:23.519
years ago when they released the

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.279
Adaptive Controller,

00:10:23.519 --> 00:10:27.360
and they used this phrase internally, is

00:10:25.279 --> 00:10:28.959
"When everybody plays we all win".

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.399
That's something that we in the

00:10:28.959 --> 00:10:31.920
community adopted,

00:10:30.399 --> 00:10:33.680
and really tried to build a showcase

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:36.399
that games are for everyone

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:39.360
and games should be for everyone, and

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:41.920
accessibility is is a huge part of that.

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:43.760
Last year we spoke to Rod Fergusson

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:45.920
of The Coalition, who went into detail

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:46.480
about Microsoft's push for

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:48.640
accessibility features

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:50.640
among its first party titles.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:52.720
You can check out that episode of Audio Logs

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:54.240
in the link below. For more information

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:56.000
on accessibility within gaming I'd

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:58.079
recommend checking out Can I Play That,

00:10:56.000 --> 00:11:00.000
which offers in-depth accessibility

00:10:58.079 --> 00:11:01.600
focused reviews of gaming hardware and

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.680
software, and there are a number of

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:06.880
charitable organizations like SpecialEffect

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:08.720
and The AbleGamers Charity dedicated to

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:11.519
enabling people with disabilities

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:12.000
to enjoy games. 

00:11:11.519 --> 00:11:19.820
For more on the past, present

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:19.820
and future of gaming keep it locked to GameSpot.

